From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:51:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: qcom: Add the Glymur USB4 DisplayPort IN adapter

On Glymur the DisplayPort stream for a USB4 tunnel comes from the msm
DisplayPort controller, which drives the router's DP IN adapter instead
of the PHY. The router firmware asks the host, as the display owner, to
allocate and release that adapter through a per-adapter request and
reply mailbox, and the host reaches the sink's DPCD through the
adapter's AUX FIFO instead of a native AUX channel.

Add a display owner for DP IN 0 of router 0:
- a worker that answers the firmware's allocate and release requests,
  hands the DP controller over to the tunnel through the msm DP USB4
  interface, and hands it back on release;
- an AUX channel over the adapter FIFO, and the control messages that
  negotiate capabilities with the far DP OUT adapter, configure the
  producer, train the link and set FEC readiness;
- a child device that exists only while a USB4 or Thunderbolt partner
  is connected, so the DRM side can defer until its connector exists
  without deferring the Type-C mux;
- save and restore of the display state around system sleep.

The display owner uses the USB4 interface of the msm DisplayPort driver
(<linux/soc/qcom/usb4-dp.h>). The adapter register layout, the reset,
link-down, clock-sync and control-completion sequences, and the mailbox
codes match what the platform's Windows driver programs on the Surface
Laptop 8.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
